; SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-SA-4.0
;
; DEED grammar, v2.0.0
; Normative for parsing. Prose and rationale: ../DEED-GRAMMAR-SPEC.adoc
;
; NOTICE (standards#837): OWNER RULING 2026-09-19 — the grammar files have
; come together: THIS is the sole normative grammar (v1.0.0), now under its
; correct extension. The v0.1.0 DRAFT archive lives at
; archive/deed.abnf_v0.1.0-draft under its true version. Its only extra rule
; (version-field) is superseded: v1.0.0 folds :schema-version into `field`
; with the "exactly once" side condition.
; Requires RFC 7405 (%s"..." case-sensitive string literals).
;
; NOTE: there is no "key = value" production and no "[section]" production.
; The only bracket is "(". A file using "=" as a field separator is not a deed.
; ("=" MAY appear INSIDE a symbol, e.g., a comparison operator.)
;
; CHANGELOG (v1.5.0 → v2.0.0, A7 rulings S1 and J24, 2026-11-14; SysArch R-01):
;   - Removed the doc-head anchor-deed and the file name ANCHOR.deed. The
;     anchor is the (anchor …) clause of the chora deed (A7 Q11, restored by
;     S1), grammared by clauses/anchor.abnf. ANCHOR.deed now dispatches to
;     nothing. NOT additive, so a major version: a v1.5.0 deed headed
;     anchor-deed, or named ANCHOR.deed, is not a v2.0.0 deed. Every other
;     v1.5.0 deed is a v2.0.0 deed. Estate files still named ANCHOR.deed are
;     folded into their repo's chora deed in that repo's own PR (A7 J25).
;
; CHANGELOG (v1.4.0 → v1.5.0, A7 ruling J17, 2026-11-13; SysArch R-03):
;   - A field may end in the bang token "!", after a separator:
;     field = keyword token-sep value [token-sep bang]. It marks a blocking
;     rule (A7 8.4). SEMANTIC (validator-enforced): it is allowed only on
;     the :id field of a (rule …) clause at the top level of a
;     contractile-deed; anywhere else it is an error. "!" could start no
;     field, clause or value before, so no v1.4.0 deed changes verdict:
;     every v1.4.0 deed is a v1.5.0 deed.
;
; CHANGELOG (v1.3.0 → v1.4.0, A7 ruling J14, 2026-11-13):
;   - Added three doc-heads, each chosen by an exact, case-sensitive file
;     name: contractile-deed (<Verb>file.deed for the six verbs),
;     descriptile-deed (the thirteen ALL-CAPS descriptile names, CLADE.deed
;     among them) and anchor-deed (ANCHOR.deed). A file in capitals says how
;     it is; a Capitalised file says how it must be (A7 YL4). mustfile.deed,
;     MUSTFILE.deed, Meta.deed and anchor.deed dispatch to nothing.
;   Additive: every v1.3.0 deed is a v1.4.0 deed. No clause syntax changes;
;   the forms these heads carry are grammared by their clause modules.
;
; CHANGELOG (v1.2.1 → v1.3.0, owner rulings U4 and I4, 2026-11-12):
;   - Added uuid (#uuid"<8-4-4-4-12 lowercase hex>"), an opaque UUID literal.
;     It carries an id minted elsewhere (the registry) as a value, not a
;     preimage to hash, so a repo move or rename never changes the deed. Only
;     versions 5 and 8 and variant 10 are legal: v4 (random) stays excluded.
;   - A line is at most 998 octets, line-end excluded, so the 8bit encoding
;     label of the deed media type is exact (RFC 2045 §2.8). Validator-
;     enforced; see the SEMANTIC note on `deed` below.
;   Additive for every deed with lines of 998 octets or fewer: every such
;   v1.2.1 deed is a v1.3.0 deed.
;   Errata, 2026-11-12 (review of #1473): uuid-variant writes "a" and "b"
;   as %s"a" / %s"b". A quoted ABNF string is case-insensitive, so the
;   first text admitted "A" and "B" there, which uuid-hex and the gate
;   refuse. No lowercase deed changes verdict.
;
; CHANGELOG (v1.2.0 → v1.2.1, owner ruling 2026-10-27):
;   - list: a token-sep MAY come before the first value. deed_lint and the
;     estate template's deed (rsr-template-repo_chora.deed) already wrote
;     multi-line lists that way. Additive: every v1.2.0 deed is a v1.2.1 deed.
;   - The gate now enforces the rest of this grammar as written: no DEL or
;     C0 control character in a string, comment or header line, a line-end
;     after every comment, and nothing between "'" and what it quotes.
;
; CHANGELOG (v1.1.0 → v1.2.0, 2026-10-16):
;   - Added exact filename 0-AI-MANIFEST.deed -> repo-deed for the canonical
;     machine front door. Existing filename dispatch and clause syntax remain.
;
; CHANGELOG (v1.0.0 → v1.1.0, owner rulings D305/D320, 2026-10-07):
;   - Added uuid8 (#u8"domain:name"), the ADR-008 profile C literal. Additive:
;     uuid5 stays legal until its own cutover, so every v1.0.0 deed is a v1.1.0 deed.
;
; CHANGELOG (v0.1.0 → v1.0.0):
;   - Added %s prefix for all case-sensitive literals (RFC 7405)
;   - Added _ to symbol continuation set
;   - Changed token-sep from WSP to SP (tabs INVALID, consistent with K9)
;   - Made version-field order-free (moved into field/clause repetition)
;   - Added EOF enforcement note
;   - Added semantic constraint notes for filename↔doc-head matching
;   - Added UUID v4 exclusion note
;   - Clarified boolean case sensitivity

deed          = header [token-sep] form [token-sep]
                ; IMPLEMENTATION NOTE: A conforming parser MUST verify
                ; that the entire input is consumed by this production.
                ; Trailing non-whitespace content after the closing ")"
                ; is a parse error.
                ; SEMANTIC (validator-enforced, v1.3.0): no line is longer
                ; than 998 octets, counted in UTF-8 bytes before its
                ; line-end (CRLF or LF). The last line counts the same way.

header        = 1*spdx-line
spdx-line     = ";;" SP %s"SPDX-" 1*text-char line-end

form          = "(" doc-head 1*(token-sep (field / clause)) [token-sep] ")"
                ; SEMANTIC: Exactly one field MUST have the keyword
                ; ":schema-version" with a string value. A conforming
                ; validator MUST reject forms lacking this field.
                ; Order of fields and clauses is otherwise not semantic.

doc-head      = %s"estate-deed"
              / %s"repo-deed"
              / %s"estate-atlas-deed"
              / %s"praxis-deed"
              / %s"contractile-deed"
              / %s"descriptile-deed"
                ; SEMANTIC CONSTRAINT: The doc-head MUST match the
                ; filename dispatch (see deed-filename below).
                ; estate_chora.deed → estate-deed
                ; ATLAS.deed        → estate-atlas-deed
                ; 0-AI-MANIFEST.deed → repo-deed
                ; *_praxis.deed     → praxis-deed
                ; *_chora.deed      → repo-deed
                ; <Verb>file.deed   → contractile-deed (J14)
                ; <NAME>.deed       → descriptile-deed (J14)
                ; A mismatch is a validation error.

; --- Filename dispatch -------------------------------------------------
; The document form is selected by the filename STEM before parsing begins.
; This production grammars the NAME, not the contents.
;
; IMPLEMENTATION NOTE: The stem is everything before the final suffix
; ("_chora.deed", "_praxis.deed", etc.). Do NOT split on "." — the
; stem may contain dots (e.g., "my.project_chora.deed" → stem "my.project").

deed-filename = estate-file / atlas-file / manifest-file
              / contractile-file / descriptile-file / praxis-file / repo-file
estate-file   = %s"estate_chora.deed"     ; -> estate-deed
atlas-file    = %s"ATLAS.deed"            ; -> estate-atlas-deed
manifest-file = %s"0-AI-MANIFEST.deed"    ; -> repo-deed
contractile-file = verb-cap %s"file.deed" ; -> contractile-deed (J14)
verb-cap      = %s"Intent" / %s"Must" / %s"Trust" / %s"Adjust" / %s"Dust" / %s"Bust"
descriptile-file = descriptile-name %s".deed" ; -> descriptile-deed (J14)
descriptile-name = %s"META" / %s"STATE" / %s"ECOSYSTEM" / %s"AGENTIC"
              / %s"NEUROSYM" / %s"PLAYBOOK" / %s"CLADE"
              / %s"INTENT" / %s"MUST" / %s"TRUST" / %s"ADJUST" / %s"DUST" / %s"BUST"
                ; Exact and case-sensitive: the case is the rule (A7 YL4).
                ; The six verb names are the verb descriptiles; CLADE is the
                ; repo's own content organisation (A7 W10), never identity.
praxis-file   = stem %s"_praxis.deed"     ; -> praxis-deed
repo-file     = stem %s"_chora.deed"      ; -> repo-deed
stem          = 1*( ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "." / "_" )

; SIDE CONDITION (normative, NOT expressible in ABNF):
; In repo-file, <stem> MUST NOT be the exact string "estate".
; The literal "estate_chora.deed" also matches repo-file, so a conforming
; implementation MUST test estate-file BEFORE repo-file and MUST NOT parse
; estate_chora.deed as a repo-deed. Dispatch is exact-stem-first.
; See ../DEED-GRAMMAR-SPEC.adoc#chora-dispatch-exclusion.
; RULED 2026-09-08 by the owner on standards#752.

field         = keyword token-sep value [token-sep bang]
bang          = "!"
                ; v1.5.0 (A7 J17). SEMANTIC (validator-enforced, not
                ; expressible here): only on the :id field of a (rule …)
                ; clause at the top level of a contractile-deed, where it
                ; marks a blocking rule (A7 8.4). Since "!" may continue a
                ; symbol, "sym!" is one symbol; the bang is "!" standing
                ; alone after a separator.
clause        = "(" symbol *(token-sep (field / clause)) [token-sep] ")"

keyword       = ":" symbol
value         = string / symbol / integer / boolean / uuid5 / uuid8 / uuid / quoted / list
list          = "(" [token-sep] [value *(token-sep value)] [token-sep] ")"
                ; A separator MAY open the list, so a multi-line list can
                ; start on the line after "(", as the estate template writes.
quoted        = "'" ( symbol / list )
                ; NOTE: Only symbols and lists may be quoted.
                ; Quoting integers, strings, or booleans is a parse error.
                ; Nothing comes between "'" and what it quotes: "' sym" is
                ; a parse error.

symbol        = ALPHA *( ALPHA / DIGIT / "." / "*" / "/" / "<" / ">"
                       / "=" / "!" / "?" / "+" / "-" / "_" )
                ; "." is STRUCTURAL: Type.Software.Library is ONE symbol
                ; whose dotted segments are meaningful to the type resolver.
                ; "=" may appear INSIDE a symbol (e.g., a comparison operator);
                ; it is never a field separator.
                ; "_" is permitted for compatibility with common identifier
                ; conventions, though hyphens are preferred in DEED keywords.

string        = DQUOTE *( str-char / escape ) DQUOTE
str-char      = %x20-21 / %x23-5B / %x5D-7E / UTF8-2 / UTF8-3 / UTF8-4
                                                    ; any char except " and \
escape        = "\" ( DQUOTE / "\" / %s"n" / %s"t" )
                ; Exactly four escapes: \" \\ \n \t
                ; \r, \uXXXX, and other escapes are INVALID.
                ; Embed non-ASCII characters directly as UTF-8.

UTF8-2        = %xC2-DF UTF8-tail
UTF8-3        = %xE0 %xA0-BF UTF8-tail / %xE1-EC 2UTF8-tail
                / %xED %x80-9F UTF8-tail / %xEE-EF 2UTF8-tail
UTF8-4        = %xF0 %x90-BF 2UTF8-tail / %xF1-F3 3UTF8-tail
                / %xF4 %x80-8F 2UTF8-tail
UTF8-tail     = %x80-BF

; Comments and SPDX payloads are UTF-8, NOT ASCII. The lexical section of the
; spec says "a deed is a sequence of UTF-8 bytes", and the header the spec
; MANDATES carries "©" (%xC2 %xA9) — which VCHAR (%x21-7E) rejects. Before
; this rule, the normative grammar rejected the specification's own example.
text-char     = VCHAR / SP / UTF8-2 / UTF8-3 / UTF8-4

integer       = [ "-" ] 1*DIGIT
                ; NOTE: Leading zeros are permitted (e.g., 007).
                ; Implementations MUST NOT interpret leading zeros as octal.

boolean       = %s"#t" / %s"#f"
                ; Strict lowercase only. #T and #F are INVALID.
                ; Never "true", "false", "yes", "no", "1", "0".

uuid5         = %s"#u5" string
                ; Body is the NAME input to RFC 4122 §4.3 under the
                ; estate namespace.
                ; NOTE: Only name-based, deterministic identifiers are supported:
                ; uuid5 here and uuid8 (profile C) below.
                ; UUID v4 (random) is intentionally excluded — all DEED
                ; identifiers MUST be reproducible from their inputs.

uuid8         = %s"#u8" string
                ; ESTATE-UUID-V8 profile C (ADR-008; D305, D320). The body is
                ; the PREIMAGE domain ":" name. The identifier is bytes 0..15
                ; of SHA-256(body) with version 8 and variant 10, so it is
                ; reproducible from the deed alone, as uuid5 is.
                ; SEMANTIC (validator-enforced): the body contains ":", and the
                ; domain before the FIRST ":" is non-empty printable ASCII
                ; (%x21-7E) — ADR-008 forbids ":" in a domain, so the first
                ; ":" always ends it. The name after it is unconstrained.
                ; Example: #u8"gv-clade-index:github.com/hyperpolymath/standards"

uuid          = %s"#uuid" DQUOTE uuid-hex DQUOTE
                ; OPAQUE UUID (v1.3.0, owner ruling U4). The body IS the
                ; identifier, in RFC 9562 form, lowercase. Nothing is hashed:
                ; a reader cannot recompute it, and the deed does not record
                ; what it was derived from. An id minted once by the registry
                ; is written this way, so a move or rename of the repo never
                ; changes the deed.
                ; Example: #uuid"b32d6be4-73ba-873e-9d61-e57f43c75cd1"
uuid-hex      = 8hex-lc "-" 4hex-lc "-" uuid-version 3hex-lc "-"
                uuid-variant 3hex-lc "-" 12hex-lc
uuid-version  = "5" / "8"
                ; Name-based only, as for uuid5 and uuid8: v4 (random) and
                ; every other version are a parse error.
uuid-variant  = "8" / "9" / %s"a" / %s"b"
                ; RFC 9562 variant 10. %s: a quoted ABNF string is
                ; case-insensitive (RFC 5234 2.3), and "A" or "B" is an error.
hex-lc        = DIGIT / %x61-66
                ; Lowercase only: "A" to "F" are a parse error.

token-sep     = 1*(SP / line-end / comment)
                ; Tabs (HTAB) are INVALID separators (consistent with K9).
                ; Use SP (0x20) for horizontal whitespace.

line-end      = CRLF / LF
comment       = ";" *text-char line-end
                ; Single ";" starts a comment (including ";;" — the second
                ; ";" is part of the comment text). Comment runs to line-end.

; Order of fields and clauses is not semantic. A canonical ordering is a
; lint convention for diffability, never a parse rule. Where precedence
; matters (rules in a praxis deed) it is carried by an explicit :priority
; INTEGER field, never by file position.
;
; The sole exception is :schema-version, which MUST be present exactly once
; in every form (enforced by the validator, not by grammar position).
